nchmark.\", \"drop_last\": {\"train\": true, \"valid\": false}, \"full_validation_samples\": 2871767, \"training\": \"scratch; official single-pass recipe adapted to DIN; sum four BCE unless declared training-loss hook\", \"baseline\": \"Initial empirical reference: DIN local activation over item-field history with action values and four separate heads; field/task adaptation, not exact original DIN reproduction\", \"research_goal\": \"Explore and validate mechanism-distinct unified modeling of multi-field user/context/target features and multi-feedback behavior histories. Develop representations and information flow that jointly support sequence modeling, feature interaction and task prediction under the fixed data and compute protocol.\", \"architecture_search\": {\"scope\": \"Whole-model design, including replacement of the initial network and all internal representations.\", \"design_dimensions\": [\"Representation units: fields, events, behavior groups, learned slots and target/task tokens.\", \"Information flow: stacked interaction, layer-wise joint interaction, parallel exchange, learned routing or other testable unified structures.\", \"History selection/compression jointly designed with target/context-conditioned retrieval.\", \"Derived features computed from authorized inputs: field matches, behavior counts/composition, grouping and sequence positions.\", \"Shared and task-conditioned representations, prediction readouts and registered training-loss mechanisms.\"], \"lineage\": \"parent_trial identifies a comparison and evidence lineage; it does not require code or architectural inheritance. inherited_components may be empty when the whole model is replaced.\", \"proposal_unit\": \"A coherent mechanism hypothesis can require several coordinated structural changes. Build that structure and plan component, replacement or factorial controls to identify where its value comes from.\", \"evidence\": \"Evaluate predictive quality, mechanism support, nearest-work d