: {\"scope\": \"Whole-model design, including replacement of the initial network and all internal representations.\", \"design_dimensions\": [\"Representation units: fields, events, behavior groups, learned slots and target/task tokens.\", \"Information flow: stacked interaction, layer-wise joint interaction, parallel exchange, learned routing or other testable unified structures.\", \"History selection/compression jointly designed with target/context-conditioned retrieval.\", \"Derived features computed from authorized inputs: field matches, behavior counts/composition, grouping and sequence positions.\", \"Shared and task-conditioned representations, prediction readouts and registered training-loss mechanisms.\"], \"lineage\": \"parent_trial identifies a comparison and evidence lineage; it does not require code or architectural inheritance. inherited_components may be empty when the whole model is replaced.\", \"proposal_unit\": \"A coherent mechanism hypothesis can require several coordinated structural changes. Build that structure and plan component, replacement or factorial controls to identify where its value comes from.\", \"evidence\": \"Evaluate predictive quality, mechanism support, nearest-work differences and measured cost. Compare new unified candidates against their closest architectural alternatives as well as the initial reference.\", \"fixed_contracts\": \"Available sample information, labels, data split, scoring, resource accounting and the frozen host training recipe remain shared. Internal architecture and readout design are candidate choices.\", \"reference_use\": \"UniRank comparison methods provide inspectable design references and nearest work. Agents choose and adapt mechanisms from local evidence.\"}, \"research_budget\": {\"seconds\": 172800, \"start_event\": \"dataset_download_and_checksum_verification_completed\", \"start_unix\": 1793959348.3455288, \"deadline_unix\": 1794132148.3455288}, \"test_policy\": \"closed during research; any final suite must be frozen before held-out scoring\", \"source_sha256\": {\"baseline.py\": \"f4b473cbacf60d72cff90f3721ad754dd617ee6065fe3fca2fc9cd4be2b25c36\", \"train.py\": \"e81bdefa140a4d78cae12f4123cc421611109c84da1b9f067e23d11b6c3d335a\", \"visibility.py\": \"d1f641c62fa3c72e1eadc03aad6d999cc9af87fceb783775eb22d1405d9ac6b4\", \"data.py\": \"ef28cb65880b6931d3e567d2bfb4a67d7530c18067b68e47bf483b65b2560438\"}, \"upstream_commit\": \"90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d\", \"benchmark_deviations\": [\"DIN is the initial empirical reference; unified research candidates can use entirely different architectures.\", \"One GPU per model; batch8192 per model (single-device rather than published distributed global batch).\", \"Click AUC selects models, four-task mean AUC is auxiliary.\", \"Validation includes every sample; upstream default drop_last may omit remainders.\", \"In-process DataLoader (num_workers=0): container shared memory is512MiB; all compared runs use the same loading policy.\", \"No torch.compile; BF16; TF32 disabled.\"], \"trial_cap_seconds\": 1203.3689693547785, \"estimated_unit_seconds\": 481.3475877419114, \"estimated_validation_seconds\": 75.22459795698524, \"frozen_unix\": 1793961097.640512, \"identity\": \"1a10f150c0b3977043072cd01f67a339c5c476f15c7847d04fa3acf9ce71e216\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
